{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## 740d CLOSED -- four orphan bugs resolved tonight\n\n2601 merged and 740d closed. Tonight's closes: 3a02, 9a17, c379, 740d.\n\n740d is worth a line because of how it was nearly mishandled: it arrived carrying two prior RCA\ncomments concluding 'host-environment artifact, no code fix warranted'. That disposition was wrong,\nand the project's own closed ticket 3476 said so verbatim -- 'the supported test suite must run both\nlocally and in CI. Treat agents dismissing reproducible local test failures as environmental noise as\nan anti-pattern.' The title's two headline claims were also both false: the refs/heads/tickets ref\nexisted fine, and safe.bareRepository shipped in git 2.38.0 (2022), so 'git 2.55.0' was a red herring.\n\nThe fix landed broader than scoped -- 8 call sites rather than the 5 the ticket named, plus a SECOND\nfile (test_tracker_footprint_cli.py) that the ticket did not know about, found by the new sweep before\nit even landed. That is the clearest evidence that replacing the hand-maintained allowlist with a\ntree-derived AST scan was the right AC to insist on: the mechanism justified itself pre-merge.\n\nRecorded honestly on the ticket: the detector was folded into the existing guard file rather than\nadded as a new scripts/check_*.py partly because of MY false claim that a mechanism-ok marker could\nnot satisfy the ratchet tests. The restructure stands on its own merits -- ticket 3476 created that\nguard for this exact rule and its allowlist WAS the defect, so repairing in place is narrower than\nadding a second mechanism beside it -- but the constraint I invented shaped the choice, and the ticket\nnow says so rather than letting the reasoning look cleaner than it was.\n\nStill in flight: 2609 (S6), 2613 (477b), 2618 (860b -- main's red), 2619 (1035, patchset 2 awaiting\nfresh review). All three of the first are LLM-Review +1 with CI queued."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788521105184054001,"uuid":"0a7aaf0c-d191-42c1-a057-f29064967583"}